<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>Environment</key>
	<string>Production</string>
	<key>GooglePlacesAPIKey</key>
	<string>YOUR_PRODUCTION_GOOGLE_PLACES_API_KEY_HERE</string>
	<key>BackendBaseURL</key>
	<string>https://api.snicolt.com</string>
	<key>EnableLogging</key>
	<false/>
	<key>EnableAnalytics</key>
	<true/>
	<key>APITimeout</key>
	<integer>15</integer>
	<key>SocketIOURL</key>
	<string>wss://socket.snicolt.com</string>
	<key>FirebaseProjectID</key>
	<string>sni-rentals-prod</string>
	<key>EnableDebugFeatures</key>
	<false/>
	<key>MockDataEnabled</key>
	<false/>
</dict>
</plist>

<!-- 
PRODUCTION CONFIGURATION
=======================

This configuration is used for the live production app.

Features:
- Optimized for performance and security
- Logging disabled to reduce overhead
- Analytics enabled for user insights
- Debug features disabled
- Mock data disabled (uses live production data)
- Fast API timeouts for better user experience

Security Notes:
1. Replace YOUR_PRODUCTION_GOOGLE_PLACES_API_KEY_HERE with production API key
2. Ensure all API keys are properly restricted in Google Cloud Console
3. Use environment variables or secure key management in CI/CD
4. This file should be committed to version control (keys should be injected)
5. Monitor API usage and set up billing alerts

Setup Instructions:
1. Configure production Firebase project
2. Set up proper API key restrictions
3. Ensure api.snicolt.com points to production backend
4. Test thoroughly in staging before deploying
-->